% Spaces common law. The configured root is the only external premise.
% Statements are native Logos compounds, paths are Logos lists, and arguments
% are native Ontos values. The @id comments name clauses for proof references.

% 1. The configured root holds every right.
% @id root-authority
authorized(R,F,S) :- root(R).

% 2. A right extends down the space path.
% @id descendant-authority
authorized(I,F,T) :- authorized(I,F,S), path_prefix(S,T).

% 3. Holding a right and being entitled to confer it are equivalent.
% @id may-confer
authorized(I,authorized(J,F,T),S) :- authorized(I,F,T).
% @id holds-underlying
authorized(I,F,T) :- authorized(I,authorized(J,F,T),S).

% 4. A counting grant confers its underlying right, within its placement.
% @id conferral
authorized(I,F,T) :- counts(A,P,authorized(I,G,U)), underlying(G,U,F,T), path_prefix(P,T).

% 5. Each supplied assertion H :- Body by A at S contributes the executable
% clause counts(A,S,H) :- Body, authorized(A,H,S). A fact has an empty Body.
% Its shared construction template is in assertion-template.logos; that
% template is specialized only for actual inputs, never installed universally.
% Input syntax and attribution are assumed valid; no publication right.

% Structural definitions implement path containment, nested-right notation and
% statement structure. They introduce no additional authority axiom.
% @id prefix-empty
path_prefix([],T).
% @id prefix-step
path_prefix([H|P],[H|T]) :- path_prefix(P,T).

% Only authorized/3 is a nested grant. Other native statement shapes terminate.
% =../2, atom/1 and ground structural inequality are standard Logos relations.
% @id underlying-grant
underlying(authorized(J,G,U),S,F,T) :- underlying(G,U,F,T).
% @id underlying-atom
underlying(F,S,F,S) :- atom(F).
% @id underlying-other
underlying(F,S,F,S) :- F =.. [P|Args], P \== authorized.
% @id underlying-zero
underlying(authorized(),S,authorized(),S).
% @id underlying-one
underlying(authorized(A),S,authorized(A),S).
% @id underlying-two
underlying(authorized(A,B),S,authorized(A,B),S).
% @id underlying-many
underlying(F,S,F,S) :- F =.. [authorized,A,B,C,D|Rest].
